Fix Other windows popover drag visibility and context menus; support bookmark dragging inside folders

- Close the Other windows popover once the overlay drag actually starts, for both docked-rail and floating-window moves. A click without movement does not dismiss it.
- Right-clicking blank space in the popover now offers New tab, New window, and the standard reopen-last-closed action instead of the popover-position menu.
- Right-clicking a popover window header/icon now opens the same window context menu as vertical mode. Its Collapse/Expand item reads and updates that popover window's own collapse state.
- Bookmark entries and folders in root folder popovers and recursively opened submenus now carry the same drag metadata as root bookmark items.
- Folder popovers are accepted as bookmark drag/drop targets, so existing bookmark-tree reorder logic also works within folders and nested folders.
- Folder popovers, submenus, and context menus are hidden while the overlay is being dragged.
- Added matching drag-source and drop-position feedback to menu-based bookmark entries.

Validation: edited JavaScript files pass syntax parsing; targeted source checks confirm nested bookmark metadata and folder-menu drop handling. No live Chrome UI test was run.
